IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clact-dates`
IMPORT `clact-claims`

-- Limitation Act 1985 (ACT), Division 4.4, s 54 and s 21BC (3) (b) -- worked cases for the questions of the person
-- bringing a claim.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and the answers used below`

`7 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 2026
`1 Jun 1993` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 1993
`15 Feb 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 2 2020
`1 Mar 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2020
`28 Feb 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2023
`1 Mar 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2023
`2 Mar 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 3 2023
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2024
`1 Jul 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2024
`30 Dec 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 12 2024
`31 Dec 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 12 2024
`1 Jan 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2025
`28 Feb 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2027
`1 Mar 2027` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2027

`a State` MEANS `the law of an Australian State`
`another Territory` MEANS `the law of another Territory`
`NZ` MEANS `the law of New Zealand`
`ACT law` MEANS `the law of the Australian Capital Territory`
`a foreign country` MEANS `the law of a country other than Australia or New Zealand`
`ACT court` MEANS `a court of the Australian Capital Territory`
`ACT arbitrator` MEANS `an arbitrator, in an arbitration held in the Australian Capital Territory`
`outside ACT` MEANS `a court or arbitrator outside the Australian Capital Territory`

`THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW` MEANS `the limitation law of the place whose law governs the claim applies to it, as part of that place's substantive law (s 56)`
`S56 NOT AN ACT COURT` MEANS `s 56 does not apply: the claim is not before a court or arbitrator of the Territory (the text's no: its "if" fails); this Act does not say which time limit applies`
`S56 ACT LAW` MEANS `s 56 does not apply: ACT law governs the claim (the text's no: its "if" fails); the time limits are this Act's own, in Parts 2 and 3 (not encoded here)`
`S56 FOREIGN LAW` MEANS `s 56 does not apply: the law of a country other than Australia or New Zealand governs the claim (the text's no: its "if" fails); this Act does not say which time limit applies (NOTHING-kind)`

`IN TIME` MEANS `in time: you began on or before the last day the limitation law of the governing place allows (s 56)`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `still in time: you have not begun, and the last day the limitation law of the governing place allows has not passed (s 56)`
`OUT OF TIME` MEANS `out of time under the limitation law of the governing place (s 56): only a discretion that law gives the court can help (see s 57)`
`NO TIME LIMIT FROM S56` MEANS `s 56 does not make another place's time limit apply on these facts (the text's no)`

`FAVOUR` MEANS `as the courts of that place do in comparable cases, and on these facts they would exercise it in your favour (s 57)`
`NOT FAVOUR` MEANS `as the courts of that place do in comparable cases, and on these facts they would not exercise it in your favour (s 57)`
`NOT PRACTICABLE` MEANS `s 57 asks the court to follow that place's courts only as far as practicable; here it is not practicable, and s 57 says no more (NOTHING-kind)`
`NO DISCRETION` MEANS `s 57 does not arise: that limitation law gives the court no discretion that you have asked it to exercise (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
`S57 NOT ACT OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE` MEANS `s 57 does not arise: not a court or arbitrator of the Territory, or not the limitation law of a State, another Territory or New Zealand (the text's no: its "if" fails)`

`the State` MEANS `an Australian State, or another Territory`
`its officer` MEANS `an officer, a Minister or an authority of an Australian State or another Territory`
`the ACT itself` MEANS `the Australian Capital Territory, or its officers or authorities`
`someone else` MEANS `someone else (the Commonwealth, a person or a company)`
`a tax` MEANS `a tax, licence fee or duty imposed, or purportedly imposed, under a law of that State or Territory`
`penalty tax` MEANS `penalty tax on such a tax, licence fee or duty`
`not tax` MEANS `something else`

`S54 BEGUN IN TIME` MEANS `yes, as far as s 54 goes: you began before that State's or Territory's relevant limitation period ended (s 54 (1) does not bar you)`
`S54 STILL IN TIME` MEANS `yes, as far as s 54 goes: you have not begun, and that State's or Territory's relevant limitation period has not ended (begin by its last day)`
`S54 BARRED` MEANS `no: that State's or Territory's relevant limitation period has ended, so the action is not maintainable (s 54 (1))`
`S54 NOT REVENUE` MEANS `s 54 does not apply: the money is not a revenue amount (s 54 (2), a "means" definition: the text's no)`
`S54 NOT A STATE` MEANS `s 54 does not apply: the action is not against another State or Territory, or its officer, Minister or authority (NOTHING-kind: s 54 says nothing about other defendants)`

§ `s 55 -- is it a limitation law`

#ASSERT `s 55 -- is it a limitation law` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 55 -- is it a limitation law` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 55 -- is it a limitation law` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 55 -- is it a limitation law` FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim`

-- Injury in a State, sued on in an ACT court: that State's limitation law.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `ACT court` `a State` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- An arbitrator in the ACT counts as "court" (s 55; fork F2); New Zealand law governs.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `ACT arbitrator` `NZ` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- Another Territory (fork F5).
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `ACT court` `another Territory` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `ACT arbitrator` `a State` EQUALS `THAT PLACE'S LIMITATION LAW`
-- ACT law governs: s 56's "if" fails; the Act's own periods.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `ACT court` `ACT law` EQUALS `S56 ACT LAW`
-- A foreign country's law: s 56's "if" fails, and the Act is silent.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `ACT court` `a foreign country` EQUALS `S56 FOREIGN LAW`
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `ACT arbitrator` `a foreign country` EQUALS `S56 FOREIGN LAW`
-- A court outside the ACT.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `outside ACT` `a State` EQUALS `S56 NOT AN ACT COURT`
-- The forum is checked before the governing law.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `outside ACT` `ACT law` EQUALS `S56 NOT AN ACT COURT`
#ASSERT `s 56 -- whose time limit applies to my claim` `outside ACT` `a foreign country` EQUALS `S56 NOT AN ACT COURT`

§ `The regulative rule alone`

-- 1 March 2020 to 1 March 2023 is 1095 days (no 29 February in between).
#ASSERT `the days from` `1 Mar 2020` `to` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS 1095
-- 1 July 2024 to 31 December 2024: 31 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 days to 1 December, then 30 more: 183.
#ASSERT `the days from` `1 Jul 2024` `to` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS 183
#ASSERT `beginning on this day is in time` 1095 0
#ASSERT `beginning on this day is in time` 1095 1094
#ASSERT `beginning on this day is in time` 1095 1095
#ASSERT NOT (`beginning on this day is in time` 1095 1096)

§ `s 56 -- am I in time`

-- Three years running from 1 March 2020; last day 1 March 2023 (the governing law's last day, a fact).
-- Begun on the last day (edge): in time.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `a State` TRUE `1 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- The day before the last day.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `a State` TRUE `28 Feb 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- The day after the last day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `a State` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- On the day time began.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `a State` TRUE `1 Mar 2020` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Before time began (fork F7: counted as day 0).
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `a State` TRUE `15 Feb 2020` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `IN TIME`
-- Not yet begun; today is the last day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `a State` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `1 Mar 2023` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
-- Not yet begun; today is the day after the last day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `a State` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `2 Mar 2023` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Not yet begun; last day still ahead.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `NZ` FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `7 Nov 2026` `29 Feb 2024` `1 Mar 2027` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
-- A period running from 29 February 2024 with a last day of 28 February 2027 (that law's counting, a fact): on it, and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT arbitrator` `another Territory` TRUE `28 Feb 2027` `7 Nov 2026` `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2027` EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT arbitrator` `another Territory` TRUE `1 Mar 2027` `7 Nov 2026` `29 Feb 2024` `28 Feb 2027` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- s 56 does not make another place's time limit apply: ACT law, a court outside, a foreign law (even when late).
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `ACT law` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM S56`
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `outside ACT` `a State` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM S56`
#ASSERT `s 56 -- am I in time` `ACT court` `a foreign country` TRUE `2 Mar 2023` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Mar 2020` `1 Mar 2023` EQUALS `NO TIME LIMIT FROM S56`

§ `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law`

#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `ACT court` `a State` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `FAVOUR`
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `ACT court` `a State` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT FAVOUR`
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `ACT court` `a State` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NOT PRACTICABLE`
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `ACT court` `a State` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `NO DISCRETION`
-- No discretion asked for is checked before practicability.
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `ACT court` `a State` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NO DISCRETION`
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `ACT arbitrator` `another Territory` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `FAVOUR`
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `ACT court` `NZ` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `NOT FAVOUR`
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `outside ACT` `a State` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S57 NOT ACT OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `ACT court` `a foreign country` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S57 NOT ACT OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `ACT court` `ACT law` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `S57 NOT ACT OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`
-- The forum and place are checked before anything else.
#ASSERT `s 57 -- how must the court use a discretion under that limitation law` `outside ACT` `a foreign country` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `S57 NOT ACT OR NOT ANOTHER PLACE`

§ `s 54 -- is it a revenue amount`

#ASSERT `s 54 -- is it a revenue amount` `a tax` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 54 -- is it a revenue amount` `penalty tax` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 54 -- is it a revenue amount` `a tax` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 54 -- is it a revenue amount` `penalty tax` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 54 -- is it a revenue amount` `not tax` TRUE)

§ `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount`

-- Duty paid 1 July 2024 under a State law said to be invalid; the State's relevant limitation period (a fact) ends
-- 31 December 2024.
-- Begun on the last day (edge): the period has not ended.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `the State` `a tax` TRUE TRUE `31 Dec 2024` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 BEGUN IN TIME`
-- The day before.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `the State` `a tax` TRUE TRUE `30 Dec 2024` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 BEGUN IN TIME`
-- The day after (edge): the period has ended.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `the State` `a tax` TRUE TRUE `1 Jan 2025` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 BARRED`
-- Against the State's officer, Minister or authority (s 54 (3)); penalty tax.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `its officer` `penalty tax` TRUE TRUE `1 Jan 2025` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 BARRED`
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `its officer` `penalty tax` TRUE TRUE `31 Dec 2024` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 BEGUN IN TIME`
-- Not yet begun: today the last day (edge), and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `the State` `a tax` TRUE FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `31 Dec 2024` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 STILL IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `the State` `a tax` TRUE FALSE `1 Jun 1993` `1 Jan 2025` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 BARRED`
-- Not a revenue amount: not paid as a tax; or not owing had the provision been valid.
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `the State` `not tax` TRUE TRUE `1 Jan 2025` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 NOT REVENUE`
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `the State` `a tax` FALSE TRUE `1 Jan 2025` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 NOT REVENUE`
-- Not against another State or Territory: s 54 is silent (the defendant is checked first).
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `the ACT itself` `a tax` TRUE TRUE `1 Jan 2025` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 NOT A STATE`
#ASSERT `s 54 -- can I still sue for the revenue amount` `someone else` `not tax` FALSE TRUE `1 Jan 2025` `7 Nov 2026` `1 Jul 2024` `31 Dec 2024` EQUALS `S54 NOT A STATE`

§ `s 21BC (3) (b) -- does the first-upload day decide the choice of law`

#ASSERT `s 21BC -- does the first-upload day decide the choice of law` TRUE EQUALS `no: the first-upload day counts only for when the limitation period begins, not for which place's law governs your defamation claim (s 21BC (2), (3) (b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 21BC -- does the first-upload day decide the choice of law` FALSE EQUALS `s 21BC does not apply: the matter was not published in electronic form (NOTHING-kind: s 21BC speaks only of the electronic rule)`
